cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite this repository."
type: software
title: "Pixel-to-Mesh Modeling for Tow-Steered Composite Laminates"

authors:
  - family-names: "Prince"
    given-names: "Md Raqibul Hasan"
  - family-names: "Dutta"
    given-names: "Soumik"
  - family-names: "Zhao"
    given-names: "Wei"

repository-code: "https://github.com/zhaowei0566/Pixel-to-Mesh-VAT-Model"
license: MIT

abstract: >-
  Source code for pixel-to-mesh modeling of tow-steered composite
  laminates manufactured using automated fiber placement.
  The framework maps individual tow images to finite elements,
  preserving local fiber orientations and the stacking sequence
  in gap and overlap regions for vibration analysis.

keywords:
  - Composite laminates
  - Automated fiber placement
  - Tow steering
  - Pixel-to-mesh modeling
  - Finite element analysis
  - Vibration analysis
